---
// Hero (epic.md §5.1a). Order: h1, lead (verbatim §3 headline), meta line,
// portrait, primary CTA, secondary, tertiary.
//
// Layout: a single-column stack below `xl`, a two-column grid at `xl` and up
// with the text in column 1 and the portrait alone in column 2. Before this,
// every child was a full-width block in a 1152px container while the lead is
// capped at a 46ch measure — so on a 1440px viewport the text stopped ~360px
// short of the container's right edge and the portrait sat underneath it,
// leaving the whole right side of the hero visibly empty.
//
// The DOM order above is preserved exactly (it's the §5.1a requirement, and
// motion.ts's `animateHero` collects `[data-animate-item]` by document order,
// so the stagger sequence depends on it). Rather than wrapping the text in a
// column div — which would force the portrait after the CTA row and change
// both the documented order and the mobile stack — each child is placed
// explicitly by grid line: text at `col-start-1` rows 1-4, portrait at
// `col-start-2` spanning those rows so it can `self-center` against the full
// text block. Only `gap-x` is set; the existing `mt-6`/`mt-8` margins still
// own the vertical rhythm, which is why the portrait needs `xl:mt-0`.
//
// Column 2 is `auto`, so the portrait's own width plus `gap-x-12` is what
// column 1 gives up — and the meta line is the binding constraint on that
// budget. At `xl` the content box is 1056px (max-w-6xl minus `xl:px-12`) and
// the meta line needs 790px to stay on one line, so column 1 must keep ~790px
// and the portrait + gap can't exceed ~266px. The default 192px portrait plus
// the 48px gap leaves column 1 at 816px, i.e. 26px of slack. That's why the
// portrait is NOT enlarged here and why there's no wider `xl` gap: both were
// tried, and either one pushes "…Machine Learning and Computer | Vision, ANU"
// onto a second line, splitting the degree name mid-phrase.
//
// That budget is also why the grid starts at `xl` (1280px) rather than `lg`
// (1024px). In the 1024-1279px band the content box is only ~960px, so a
// side-by-side 192px portrait leaves column 1 at ~722px and the meta line
// wraps no matter how the gap is tuned — a regression, since that band renders
// it on one line today. Keeping those widths stacked means no width loses
// anything, and `xl` still covers every common laptop (1366, 1440, 1536,
// 1920); what stays stacked is tablet-landscape, where a stack is right anyway.
//
// Motion: the four elements epic.md §8.3 names (h1, lead, meta line, CTA
// row) drive the on-load stagger — the portrait is deliberately NOT in that
// inventory, so it renders statically. The primary "Email me" button is
// deliberately pulled OUT of the animated CTA-row wrapper and always
// renders at full opacity: it's both the single highest-priority element on
// the page (no reason to ever delay it) and the one accent-filled control
// whose text needs a strict 4.5:1 contrast a mid-fade opacity blend can't
// reliably hold — see updates/002.md. The secondary/tertiary links still
// fade in together as their own beat. The meta line uses `--text` rather
// than `--text-muted` for the same reason: it's one of the four elements
// that MUST animate per epic.md §8.3's hero inventory (h1, lead, meta line,
// CTA row), so unlike the marginal-contrast meta strips pruned from
// animation elsewhere, it can't just be left static — `--text` has enough
// contrast headroom (16-18:1 at rest) to survive being sampled at any
// point in the fade.
import { hero } from '../data/site';
import Portrait from './Portrait.astro';
---

<section
  id="hero"
  data-animate="hero"
  class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24 xl:grid xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] xl:items-start xl:gap-x-12 xl:px-12"
>
  <h1 data-animate-item class="text-display text-text xl:col-start-1 xl:row-start-1">{hero.h1}</h1>
  <p data-animate-item class="text-hero-lead mt-6 text-text xl:col-start-1 xl:row-start-2">
    {hero.lead}
  </p>
  <p data-animate-item class="text-meta mt-6 text-text xl:col-start-1 xl:row-start-3">
    {hero.metaLine}
  </p>

  <div class="mt-8 xl:col-start-2 xl:row-span-4 xl:row-start-1 xl:mt-0 xl:self-center xl:justify-self-end">
    <Portrait />
  </div>

  <div
    class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-4 xl:col-start-1 xl:row-start-4"
  >
    <a href={hero.ctaPrimary.href} class="btn-primary">{hero.ctaPrimary.label}</a>
    <div data-animate-item class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-4">
      <a href={hero.ctaSecondary.href} class="link-quiet text-sm font-medium"
        >{hero.ctaSecondary.label}</a
      >
      {
        hero.ctaTertiary.map((link) => (
          <a href={link.href} class="link-quiet text-sm font-medium" rel="noopener">
            {link.label}
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
